{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.88,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": [
        "D31"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "D31.1",
        "D31.2",
        "D31.3",
        "D31.4"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "VOUTP",
        "VOUTN",
        "NET0162",
        "NET0183"
      ],
      "observed": "D31 is listed as a two-pin LED_GREEN part (Device LED, LED_0805 footprint), but the netlist connects D31 to four pins/nets: pin 1 to VOUTP, pin 2 to VOUTN, pin 3 to NET0162, and pin 4 to NET0183. This is the same four-pin bridge-rectifier topology used by D49.",
      "expected": "A two-pin LED should only have pins 1 and 2 and should not occupy a four-pin bridge position. The D31 location should be a four-pin bridge rectifier (such as ABS2, like D49), or D31 should be removed if it is truly an LED.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"D31\") (value \"LED_GREEN\") (footprint \"LED_SMD:LED_0805_2012Metric\") ... (libsource (lib \"Device\") (part \"LED\") (description \"Light emitting diode\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"223\") (name \"VOUTP\") ... (node (ref \"D31\") (pin \"1\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"222\") (name \"VOUTN\") ... (node (ref \"D31\") (pin \"2\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"122\") (name \"NET0162\") ... (node (ref \"D31\") (pin \"3\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"129\") (name \"NET0183\") ... (node (ref \"D31\") (pin \"4\") ...))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"D49\") (value \"ABS2\") (footprint \"Diode_SMD:Diode_Bridge_Diotec_ABS\") ... (libsource (lib \"Diode_Bridge\") (part \"ABS2\") ...))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If D31 is assembled as an LED, the four-pin bridge path cannot be implemented and the transformer center-tap/VOUTP/VOUTN circuit is open or misconnected. If the nets are forced together, an LED may short or bias VOUTP/VOUTN. In either case the board will not behave as the intended four-pin bridge/transformer common-mode path.",
      "confidence": 0.92
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a clear component-type anomaly: D31 is specified as a two-pin LED but is connected as a four-pin bridge rectifier, unlike the correct D49 ABS2 bridge. This would change the Ethernet/transformer power or common-mode path and is the main deviation from the intended design."
}

